# Keep demo login chips + reset

The login page has click-to-fill demo accounts and a red **Clear all data & reset**
button. Both are intentional for local DEV and current demo/staging deploys.

## Do not remove unless the user explicitly asks

Never remove or disable any of the following without an explicit user request:

- `DEV_ACCOUNTS` / `DEV_PASSWORD` / `fillDevAccount` / the demo-accounts UI block in `frontend/src/pages/LoginPage.tsx`
- The red `Clear all data & reset` button (shown whenever `SHOW_DEMO_ACCOUNTS` is on)
- `SHOW_DEMO_ACCOUNTS` / `VITE_SHOW_DEMO_ACCOUNTS` gating
- `VITE_SHOW_DEMO_ACCOUNTS=true` in `frontend/package.json` `"build"` script
- `VITE_SHOW_DEMO_ACCOUNTS=true` / `MITO_ALLOW_DEV_RESET=1` in ops/staging env examples
- Backend `/api/dev/reset/` wiring via `DEBUG` or `MITO_ALLOW_DEV_RESET`

## Deploy / build

- Default SPA build (`npm run build`) must keep demo chips + reset button visible.
- Demo/staging deploys with `DJANGO_DEBUG=false` must set `MITO_ALLOW_DEV_RESET=1` so the red button works.
- `npm run build:no-demo` exists only for an explicit “strip demo login” request.
- Empty username/password placeholders are fine; do not confuse those with demo chips.

## When the user does ask to remove

Only then: drop chips/reset UI and/or stop setting `VITE_SHOW_DEMO_ACCOUNTS` / `MITO_ALLOW_DEV_RESET`, and use `build:no-demo` (or equivalent) for production.
